{
  "dom_id": "questionContainer",
  "name": "Question 74",
  "problem": "A random variable $X$ has the probability distribution given below.\n\n| $x$ | $-4$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ | $0.2$ | $0.5$ |\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[1-4X].$",
  "worked_solution": "First, let's find $\\text{E}[X].$ \n\nThe expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ and sample space $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x) \\\\  & =-4\\cdot 0.05-3\\cdot 0.1-2\\cdot 0.15-1\\cdot 0.2+0\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[1-4X] & =\\text{E}[-4X+1] \\\\  & =-4\\text{E}[X]+1 \\\\  & =-4\\cdot (-1)+1 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
